[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi!<br>\nConsider the following code:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Piece</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pawn</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Rook</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Knight</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Queen</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bishop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">King</span>\n<span class=\"n\">deriving</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">inline</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Piece</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fromUInt8</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UInt8</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Piece</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pawn</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Rook</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Knight</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Queen</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bishop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">King</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exfalso</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--works</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exfalso</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fails</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The last two branches of the match-statement in the <code>Piece.fromUInt8</code> function can't be reached, because of <code>h</code>. When i provide an explicit value (for example 6), grind can figure out a contradiction with <code>h</code>. But when i use a catch-all statement, this doesn't work.<br>\n Is it possible to get a hypothesis (like <code>h : x != 0 \\and x != 1 etc.</code>)that I am not in any of the previous branches in the last line?</p>",
        "id": 596970284,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Krause",
        "timestamp": 1779446426
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><del>replace <code>x</code> by <code>x+6</code> and it will likely work</del>. (At least: it would work if <code>i : Nat</code>, maybe it's different for <code>UInt8</code>)</p>",
        "id": 596986495,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1779451402
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This gives me the error: </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>Invalid pattern(s): `x` is an explicit pattern variable, but it only occurs in positions that are inaccessible to pattern matching:\n  {\n    toBitVec :=\n      {\n        toFin :=\n          ⟨.(Decidable.rec (fun h =&gt; (fun x_1 =&gt; (x.toBitVec.toNat + 5).succ) h)\n                (fun h =&gt; (fun x_1 =&gt; (x.toBitVec.toNat + 5).succ.modCore (2 ^ 8)) h)\n                ((2 ^ 8).decLe (x.toBitVec.toNat + 5).succ)),\n            ⋯⟩ } }\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But when I do <code>i.toNat</code>, it works.</p>",
        "id": 596987110,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Krause",
        "timestamp": 1779451586
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The point of this function is to be fast and use unboxed values. Would using repeated if-statements with UInt8 be slower than pattern matching on i.Nat?</p>",
        "id": 596987463,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Krause",
        "timestamp": 1779451670
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm afraid I don't have enough/any experience with <code>UInt8</code> to be able to answer those questions, so hopefully someone else can.</p>",
        "id": 596987810,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1779451754
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"652766\">Christian Krause</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/prove.20that.20match.20branch.20is.20unreachable/near/596987463\">schrieb</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Would using repeated if-statements with UInt8 be slower than pattern matching on i.Nat?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>No, I don’t think so</p>",
        "id": 597015694,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1779459025
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here is a workaround:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Piece</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pawn</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Rook</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Knight</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Queen</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bishop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">King</span>\n<span class=\"n\">deriving</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">inline</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Piece</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fromUInt8</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UInt8</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Piece</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toNat</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pawn</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Rook</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Knight</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Queen</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bishop</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">King</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>And I suggest you actually benchmark before using <code>UInt8</code> over <code>Int</code>, it may not make the difference you think it makes.</p>",
        "id": 597015927,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1779459087
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I am using UInt8 because I have a lot of arrays where I need to store Squares:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Square</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UInt8</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">wellFormed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Square</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pieceBits</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp_all</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Square</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pieceBits</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">decide</span>\n<span class=\"n\">deriving</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This raises another question actually, how can I check that the values in the array <code>Vector Square 64</code> are actually unboxed (as I hope them to be)?</p>",
        "id": 597045986,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Krause",
        "timestamp": 1779466393
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Another question: When looking at the IR files genereated in <code>.lake/build</code>,  my (naive) search finds no match statements, only some functions with <code>_match__n_</code> splitter in the name. Is there documentation how lean match statements are handled under the hood?</p>",
        "id": 597046943,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Krause",
        "timestamp": 1779466676
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"652766\">Christian Krause</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/prove.20that.20match.20branch.20is.20unreachable/near/597045986\">schrieb</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>how can I check that the values in the array <code>Vector Square 64</code> are actually unboxed (as I hope them to be)?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>You are too optimistic :-). <code>Vector</code> does not unbox. But small <code>Nat</code>s and small enums (like <code>Piece</code>) are represented tagged, so there will be no pointer indirection, but still 8 words per entry.</p>",
        "id": 597130277,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1779472856
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ohh, thats a bit disappointing. Are there technical limitations that prevent this Unboxing or is this just high-priority for the FRO? </p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>But small Nats and small enums (like Piece) are represented tagged, </p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>And what does being \"tagged\" mean?</p>",
        "id": 597132256,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Krause",
        "timestamp": 1779473392
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"652766\">Christian Krause</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/prove.20that.20match.20branch.20is.20unreachable/near/597132256\">schrieb</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Are there technical limitations that prevent this Unboxing</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>It makes the representation of <code>Vector</code> non-uniform and you cannot have polymorphic code (like <code>Vector.map</code>) without specialization.</p>\n<p>tagged means that a scalar value is stored in a place where usually a pointer is. The tag is the last bit, this tells the system that this is not a pointer. A bit of documentation is found at <a href=\"https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/latest/Run-Time-Code/Boxing/#boxing\">https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/latest/Run-Time-Code/Boxing/#boxing</a> and <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/ydewit/7ab62be1bd0fea5bd53b48d23914dd6b\">https://gist.github.com/ydewit/7ab62be1bd0fea5bd53b48d23914dd6b</a> looks interesting</p>",
        "id": 597139567,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1779475548
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That's interesting, thank you for the reference :-)</p>",
        "id": 597306709,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Krause",
        "timestamp": 1779540879
    }
]